# KYC name matching

This codebase verifies whether two extracted Indian POI/POA name strings (PAN, Aadhaar, passport, DL, voter ID) refer to the same person.

- False positive = two different people auto-approved (fraud). Worse than a false negative (same person → reviewer).
- Primary metric: F0.5. Do not trade precision for recall without saying so.
- Think in **first / middle / last** name components, not bag-of-characters.
- Read `docs/kyc-business-context.md` before changing labels or matchers.

Project skills (invoke by name or when the task matches):

- `.cursor/skills/kyc-data-alignment/SKILL.md` — keep ~30% match / 70% non-match with first/middle/last
- `.cursor/skills/kyc-matching-strategy/SKILL.md` — token_overlap + structured_fields only
- `.cursor/skills/kyc-pr-review/SKILL.md` — PR review for this repo
